==== gls_nofr
gls_nofr(X::n×m, M::n×n spd, y::n)
  potrf    L1 ← chol(M)                      M = L1 L1ᵀ, Cholesky
  copy     T1 ← X
  trsm     T1 ← L1⁻¹ T1
  syrk     T2 ← T1ᵀ T1                       one triangle only
  symm.    T2 ← sym(T2)                      copy one triangle to the other
  getrf    LU1 ← lu(T2)                      P T2 = L U, LU
  trsv     T3 ← L1⁻¹ y
  gemv     T4 ← T1ᵀ T3
  getrs    T4 ← LU1⁻¹ T4
  return T4
if a factorisation fails, the call throws InfoError with
  info 1:  Cholesky factorisation of M: not positive definite
  info 2:  LU factorisation of a computed matrix: singular

result: [1.2739726027397262, 0.9452054794520547]
==== gls_nospd
gls_nospd(X::n×m full_rank, M::n×n, y::n)
  getrf    LU1 ← lu(M)                       P M = L U, LU
  getrs    T1 ← LU1⁻ᵀ X
  gemm     T2 ← T1ᵀ X
  getrf    LU2 ← lu(T2)                      P T2 = L U, LU
  gemv     T3 ← T1ᵀ y
  getrs    T3 ← LU2⁻¹ T3
  return T3
if a factorisation fails, the call throws InfoError with
  info 1:  LU factorisation of M: singular
  info 2:  LU factorisation of a computed matrix: singular

result: [1.2739726027397262, 0.9452054794520547]
==== gls_sym
gls_sym(X::n×m full_rank, M::n×n symmetric, y::n)
  getrf    LU1 ← lu(M)                       P M = L U, LU
  getrs    T1 ← LU1⁻ᵀ X
  gemmtr   T2 ← T1ᵀ X                        symmetric: one triangle only
  symm.    T2 ← sym(T2)                      copy one triangle to the other
  getrf    LU2 ← lu(T2)                      P T2 = L U, LU
  gemv     T3 ← T1ᵀ y
  getrs    T3 ← LU2⁻¹ T3
  return T3
if a factorisation fails, the call throws InfoError with
  info 1:  LU factorisation of M: singular
  info 2:  LU factorisation of a computed matrix: singular

result: [1.2739726027397262, 0.9452054794520547]
==== gls_assume
gls_assume(X::n×m, M::n×n spd, y::n)
  potrf    L1 ← chol(M)                      M = L1 L1ᵀ, Cholesky
  copy     T1 ← X
  trsm     T1 ← L1⁻¹ T1
  syrk     T2 ← T1ᵀ T1                       one triangle only
  potrf    L2 ← chol(T2)                     T2 = L2 L2ᵀ, Cholesky
  trsv     T3 ← L1⁻¹ y
  gemv     T4 ← T1ᵀ T3
  trsv     T4 ← L2⁻¹ T4
  trsv     T4 ← L2⁻ᵀ T4
  return T4
if a factorisation fails, the call throws InfoError with
  info 1:  Cholesky factorisation of M: not positive definite
  info 2:  Cholesky factorisation of a computed matrix: not positive definite

result: [1.2739726027397262, 0.9452054794520546]
==== iterate
iterate(M::n×n spd, x0::n, steps::Index)
  potrf    L1 ← chol(M)                      M = L1 L1ᵀ, Cholesky
  copy     x ← x0                            the loop's state, in place
  for i = 0:steps-1
    trsv     x ← L1⁻¹ x
    trsv     x ← L1⁻ᵀ x
  return x
if a factorisation fails, the call throws InfoError with
  info 1:  Cholesky factorisation of M: not positive definite

